<p dir=3D"auto">There are three ways to apply CSS to HTML: Inline, internal=
, and external.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Inline CSS:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Inline CSS is specified directly in the opening tag of the =
element you want it to apply to. It is entered into the style attribute wit=
hin HTML. This allows CSS properties on a "per tag" basis.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-rela=
