<p dir=3D"auto">This CSS type is not really recommended, as each HTML tag n=
eeds to be styled individually. However, inline CSS in HTML can be useful i=
n some situations. For example, in cases where you don't have access to CSS=
 files or need to apply styles for a single element only.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Internal CSS:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Internal or Embedded, styles are used for the whole page. I=
nside the head element, the style tags surround all of the styles for the p=
age.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
