<p dir=3D"auto">The CSS box model is a rectangular layout paradigm for HTML=
 elements that consists of the following:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Content</strong>: The content of the box, where text and images=
 appear</li>
<li><strong>Padding</strong>: A transparent area surrounding the content (i=
.e., the amount of space between the border and the content)</li>
<li><strong>Border</strong>: A border surrounding the padding (if any) and =
content</li>
<li><strong>Margin</strong>: A transparent area surrounding the border (i.e=
., the amount of space between the border and any neighboring elements)</li=
>
</ul>
<p align=3D"center" dir=3D"auto">
  <a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://github.c=
om/learning-zone/css-basics/blob/master/assets/images/box-model.png"><img s=
rc=3D"https://github.com/learning-zone/css-basics/raw/master/assets/images/=
box-model.png" alt=3D"CSS Box Model" width=3D"300px;" style=3D"max-width: 1=
00%;"></a>
</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The size of the box itself is calculated like this:</p>
