<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Margin collapsing</strong> occurs when the top and =
bottom margins of block-level elements combine into a single margin equal t=
o the <strong>larger</strong> of the two values.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Scenarios where margin collapsing occurs:</strong><=
/p>
