<p dir=3D"auto">A <strong>contextual selector</strong> targets an element o=
nly when it appears within a specific context (ancestor). It's a string of =
selectors separated by whitespace, where only the last element is styled =
=E2=80=94 but only if it matches the specified ancestral path.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
