<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Relative Position</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">An element with <code>position: relative;</code> is positio=
ned relative to its normal position.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Setting the top, right, bottom, and left properties of a re=
latively-positioned element will cause it to be adjusted away from its norm=
al position. Other content will not be adjusted to fit into any gap left by=
 the element.</p>
