<p dir=3D"auto"><code>position: sticky</code> is a hybrid between <code>rel=
ative</code> and <code>fixed</code>. The element is positioned relative to =
the normal flow until it crosses a specified threshold (e.g., <code>top: 0<=
/code>), at which point it "sticks" and behaves like <code>position: fixed<=
/code> <strong>within its scroll container</strong>.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre>.<span class=3D"pl-c1">sticky-header</span=
