<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th><code>sticky</code></th>
<th><code>fixed</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Stays in document flow</td>
<td><strong>Yes</strong> =E2=80=94 occupies original space</td>
<td>No =E2=80=94 removed from flow</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Constrained to parent</td>
<td><strong>Yes</strong> =E2=80=94 stops sticking when parent scrolls away<=
/td>
<td>No =E2=80=94 always relative to viewport</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Needs offset property</td>
<td>Yes (<code>top</code>, <code>left</code>, etc.)</td>
<td>Yes</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common pitfalls:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong><code>overflow: hidden</code> or <code>overflow: auto</code> on=
 an ancestor breaks sticky.</strong> The sticky element scrolls with the ov=
erflow container, not the viewport.</li>
</ol>
