<p dir=3D"auto">These three properties control how a flex item sizes itself=
 relative to the available space in the flex container. The <code>flex</cod=
e> shorthand combines all three.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>flex-grow</code></td>
<td><code>0</code></td>
<td>How much the item <strong>grows</strong> relative to others when extra =
space is available</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>flex-shrink</code></td>
<td><code>1</code></td>
<td>How much the item <strong>shrinks</strong> relative to others when spac=
e is insufficient</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>flex-basis</code></td>
<td><code>auto</code></td>
<td>The <strong>initial main size</strong> of the item before growing/shrin=
king</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
