<p dir=3D"auto">Both are used with <code>repeat()</code> and <code>minmax()=
</code> to create <strong>intrinsically responsive grids</strong> without m=
edia queries. The difference lies in how they handle empty tracks.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th><code>auto-fill</code></th>
<th><code>auto-fit</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Empty columns</td>
<td>Kept =E2=80=94 adds extra empty tracks to fill the row</td>
<td><strong>Collapsed</strong> to 0 width</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Items stretch to fill row</td>
<td>No</td>
<td><strong>Yes</strong> =E2=80=94 existing items expand</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Best for</td>
<td>Fixed-size item grids</td>
<td>Fluid grids where items should fill available space</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
