<p dir=3D"auto"><code>:is()</code> (also known as the "matches" pseudo-clas=
s) accepts a selector list and matches any element that can be matched by o=
ne of the selectors in the list. It reduces repetition and simplifies compl=
ex selector groups.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Specificity:</strong> <code>:is()</code> takes the =
specificity of its <strong>most specific</strong> argument.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">/* Without :is() =E2=
=80=94 repetitive */</span>
<span class=3D"pl-ent">header</span> <span class=3D"pl-ent">h1</span><span =
class=3D"pl-kos">,</span> <span class=3D"pl-ent">header</span> <span class=
