<p dir=3D"auto"><code>:where()</code> works identically to <code>:is()</cod=
e> in terms of matching elements, but it always has <strong>zero specificit=
y</strong>. This makes it useful for applying base or default styles that a=
re easy to override.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
