<p dir=3D"auto"><code>::selection</code> applies styles to the portion of a=
 document that has been highlighted (selected) by the user, such as by clic=
king and dragging over text.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Supported CSS properties</strong> (only a subset is=
 allowed):</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><code>color</code></li>
<li><code>background-color</code></li>
<li><code>text-shadow</code></li>
<li><code>text-decoration</code> (in some browsers)</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">/* Custom selection c=
olor for the whole page */</span>
::<span class=3D"pl-c1">selection</span> {
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">background-color</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</sp=
an> <span class=3D"pl-pds"><span class=3D"pl-kos">#</span>3498db</span>;
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">color</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</span> <span c=
lass=3D"pl-pds"><span class=3D"pl-kos">#</span>ffffff</span>;
}

<span class=3D"pl-c">/* Different selection color inside a specific element=
 */</span>
.<span class=3D"pl-c1">highlight-section</span>::<span class=3D"pl-c1">sele=
ction</span> {
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">background-color</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</sp=
an> <span class=3D"pl-pds"><span class=3D"pl-kos">#</span>f39c12</span>;
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">color</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</span> <span c=
lass=3D"pl-pds"><span class=3D"pl-kos">#</span>000</span>;
}</pre><div class=3D"zeroclipboard-container">
