<p dir=3D"auto"><code>animation-fill-mode</code> controls what styles are a=
pplied to an element before the animation starts and after it ends.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Value</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>none</code></td>
<td>Default. No styles are applied outside the animation's active period</t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>forwards</code></td>
<td>Element retains the styles of the <strong>last</strong> keyframe after =
the animation ends</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>backwards</code></td>
<td>Element applies the styles of the <strong>first</strong> keyframe durin=
g the delay period</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>both</code></td>
<td>Applies both <code>forwards</code> and <code>backwards</code> behaviour=
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
