<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When to use:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Only apply it to elements that will <strong>definitely</strong> animate=
 (not as a blanket performance fix).</li>
<li>Remove it after the animation is complete (via JavaScript) to free GPU =
memory.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common values:</strong> <code>auto</code>, <code>tr=
ansform</code>, <code>opacity</code>, <code>scroll-position</code>, or any =
other animatable CSS property.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Warning:</strong> Overusing <code>will-change</code=
> can harm performance by consuming excessive memory. Apply it sparingly.</=
p>
</blockquote>
