<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>perspective</code> property gives a 3D-positioned=
 element some perspective by defining the distance between the viewer (z=3D=
0 plane) and the element. A smaller value creates a more dramatic 3D effect=
; a larger value makes it subtler.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">It can be applied in two ways:</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>On the parent</strong> using <code>perspective</code> property =
=E2=80=94 affects all 3D-transformed children.</li>
<li><strong>On the element itself</strong> using <code>transform: perspecti=
ve()</code> function =E2=80=94 affects only that element.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">/* Applied on parent =
=E2=80=94 shared perspective for all children */</span>
.<span class=3D"pl-c1">scene</span> {
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">perspective</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</span> <=
span class=3D"pl-c1">500<span class=3D"pl-smi">px</span></span>;
}

.<span class=3D"pl-c1">box</span> {
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">transform</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</span> <sp=
an class=3D"pl-en">rotateY</span>(<span class=3D"pl-c1">45<span class=3D"pl=
-smi">deg</span></span>);
}

<span class=3D"pl-c">/* Applied on element itself */</span>
.<span class=3D"pl-c1">box-self</span> {
  <span class=3D"pl-c1">transform</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</span> <sp=
an class=3D"pl-en">perspective</span>(<span class=3D"pl-c1">500<span class=
=3D"pl-smi">px</span></span>) <span class=3D"pl-en">rotateY</span>(<span cl=
ass=3D"pl-c1">45<span class=3D"pl-smi">deg</span></span>);
}</pre><div class=3D"zeroclipboard-container">
