<p dir=3D"auto">A CSS framework provides pre-written styles, components, an=
d layout utilities to accelerate UI development and enforce consistency.</p=
>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Two primary approaches:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Approach</th>
<th>Examples</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Component-based</strong></td>
<td>Bootstrap, Foundation, Bulma</td>
<td>Pre-built UI components (cards, navbars, modals) with an opinionated de=
sign.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Utility-first</strong></td>
<td>Tailwind CSS, Tachyons</td>
<td>Atomic single-purpose utility classes applied directly in HTML; no pre-=
built look.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
