<p dir=3D"auto">Custom properties (sometimes referred to as <strong>CSS var=
iables</strong> or <strong>cascading variables</strong>) are entities defin=
ed by CSS authors that contain specific values to be reused throughout a do=
cument. They are set using custom property notation (e.g., <code>--main-col=
or: black;</code>) and are accessed using the <code>var()</code> function (=
e.g., <code>color: var(--main-color);</code>).</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Property names that are prefixed with <code>--</code>, like=
 <code>--example-name</code>, represent custom properties that contain a va=
lue that can be used in other declarations using the <code>var()</code> fun=
ction.</p>
