<p dir=3D"auto">Both properties control how long words or URLs break across=
 lines, but with subtle differences.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong><code>word-break</code></strong>: Controls where li=
ne breaks occur within a word.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Value</th>
<th>Behavior</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>normal</code></td>
<td>Default; breaks at allowed break points</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>break-all</code></td>
<td>Breaks at any character (even mid-word) to prevent overflow</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>keep-all</code></td>
<td>No mid-word breaks (used for CJK text)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong><code>overflow-wrap</code></strong> (formerly <code=
>word-wrap</code>): Only breaks a word if it would overflow the container.<=
/p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
