<p dir=3D"auto">Both control transparency, but they differ in scope:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th><code>opacity</code></th>
<th><code>rgba()</code> / <code>hsla()</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Affects</td>
<td>The <strong>entire element</strong> and all its children</td>
<td>Only the <strong>specific property</strong> it is applied to</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Children</td>
<td>Children inherit the transparency and cannot override it</td>
<td>Children are unaffected</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Stacking context</td>
<td>Creates a new stacking context</td>
<td>Does not create a stacking context</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Values</td>
<td><code>0</code> (invisible) to <code>1</code> (fully visible)</td>
<td>Alpha channel <code>0</code>=E2=80=93<code>1</code> in color functions<=
/td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
