<p dir=3D"auto"><code>object-fit</code> controls how a <strong>replaced ele=
ment</strong> (<code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>) fills =
its container, similar to how <code>background-size</code> works for backgr=
ound images.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Value</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>fill</code></td>
<td>Default =E2=80=94 stretches to fill the box, may distort aspect ratio</=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>contain</code></td>
<td>Scales to fit <strong>inside</strong> the box, preserving aspect ratio =
(letterbox)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>cover</code></td>
<td>Scales to <strong>cover</strong> the box, preserving aspect ratio (may =
crop)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>none</code></td>
<td>Keeps the image at its natural size</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>scale-down</code></td>
<td>Behaves as <code>none</code> or <code>contain</code>, whichever is smal=
ler</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
