<p dir=3D"auto"><code>mix-blend-mode</code> defines how an element's conten=
t blends with the content <strong>behind it</strong> (its backdrop and pare=
nt's background). It works like Photoshop blending modes applied in CSS.</p=
>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common values:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Value</th>
<th>Effect</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>normal</code></td>
<td>Default =E2=80=94 no blending</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>multiply</code></td>
<td>Darkens =E2=80=94 multiplies color channels (like overlaying transparen=
cies)</td>
</tr>
