<p dir=3D"auto">When <code>overflow</code> is set to any value other than <=
code>visible</code> (e.g. <code>hidden</code>, <code>scroll</code>, <code>a=
uto</code>), the element establishes a <strong>Block Formatting Context (BF=
C)</strong>. This has several useful side effects:</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Clears floats</strong> =E2=80=94 the BFC container expands to c=
ontain floated children.</li>
<li><strong>Prevents margin collapse</strong> =E2=80=94 margins of children=
