<p dir=3D"auto">CSS masking uses an image, gradient, or SVG element as a <s=
trong>mask layer</strong>. Only the parts of the element where the mask is =
opaque (alpha masking) or bright (luminance masking) are visible =E2=80=94 =
enabling <strong>soft edges</strong> and partial transparency that <code>cl=
ip-path</code> cannot produce.</p>
