<p dir=3D"auto">The BEM (<strong>Block Element Modifier</strong>) methodolo=
gy is a naming convention for CSS classes in order to keep CSS more maintai=
nable by defining namespaces to solve scoping issues. A Block is a standalo=
ne component that is reusable across projects and acts as a "namespace" for=
 sub components (Elements). Modifiers are used as flags when a Block or Ele=
ment is in a certain state or is different in structure or style.</p>
