<p dir=3D"auto">The pose-to-pose option is to create a few keyframes throug=
hout the sequence, and then fill in the gaps later. Filling in these gaps i=
s known as <strong>tweening</strong>. It is the process of generating inter=
mediate frames between two images. It gives the impression that the first i=
mage has smoothly evolved into the second one. In CSS3, Transforms (matrix,=
 translate, rotate, scale etc.) module can be used to achieve tweening.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-ent">p</span> {
