<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>opacity</code> CSS property sets the opacity of a=
n element. Opacity is the degree to which content behind an element is hidd=
en, and is the opposite of transparency.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative =
overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-ent">div</span> { <span =
class=3D"pl-c1">background-color</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">:</span> ligh=
tblue; }
