<p dir=3D"auto">There are various units in CSS to express the measurement a=
nd length. A CSS unit is used to determine the property size, which we set =
for an element or its content. The units in CSS are required to define the =
measurement such as margin: 20px; in which the px (or pixel) is the CSS uni=
t. They are used to set margin, padding, lengths, and so on.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The length unit in CSS is of two types:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Absolute length units.</li>
<li>Relative length units.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Absolute length units:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The following are all absolute length units =E2=80=94 they =
are not relative to anything else, and are generally considered to always b=
e the same size.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Unit</th>
<th>Name</th>
<th>Equivalent to</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>cm</td>
<td>Centimeters</td>
<td>1cm =3D 38px =3D 25/64in</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>mm</td>
<td>Millimeters</td>
<td>1mm =3D 1/10th of 1cm</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Q</td>
<td>Quarter-millimeters</td>
<td>1Q =3D 1/40th of 1cm</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>in</td>
<td>Inches</td>
<td>1in =3D 2.54cm =3D 96px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>pc</td>
<td>Picas</td>
<td>1pc =3D 1/6th of 1in</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>pt</td>
<td>Points</td>
<td>1pt =3D 1/72th of 1in</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>px</td>
<td>Pixels</td>
<td>1px =3D 1/96th of 1in</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Relative length units:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Relative length units specify a length relative to another =
length property. Relative length units scale better between different rende=
ring medium.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Unit</th>
<th>Relative to</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>em</td>
<td>Font size of the parent, in the case of typographical properties like f=
ont-size, and font size of the element itself, in the case of other propert=
ies like width.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>ex</td>
<td>x-height of the element's font.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>ch</td>
<td>The advance measure (width) of the glyph "0" of the element's font.</td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>rem</td>
<td>Font size of the root element.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>lh</td>
<td>Line height of the element.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>vw</td>
<td>1% of the viewport's width.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>vh</td>
<td>1% of the viewport's height.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>vmin</td>
<td>1% of the viewport's smaller dimension.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>vmax</td>
<td>1% of the viewport's larger dimension.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
