<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Node Relationships</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The nodes in the DOM Document have a hierarchical relations=
hip to each other. This means that the nodes are structured like a tree. We=
 use the terms parent, sibling and child to describe the relationship betwe=
en nodes.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The top node is called the root and is the only node that h=
as no parent. The root in a normal HTML document is the <code>&lt;html/&gt;=
</code> tag because it has no parent and is the top tag of the document.</p=
>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Navigating Between Nodes</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">We can navigate between nodes using these properties:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>parentNode</li>
<li>childNodes</li>
<li>firstChild</li>
<li>lastChild</li>
<li>nextSibling</li>
</ul>
