<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>PostCSS</strong> is a tool that processes CSS using=
 JavaScript plugins. Unlike Sass/Less =E2=80=94 which introduce their own s=
yntax and compile it to CSS =E2=80=94 PostCSS works on <strong>standard CSS=
</strong> and transforms it via a plugin pipeline.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th>Sass / Less / Stylus</th>
<th>PostCSS</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Input syntax</td>
<td>Custom (<code>.scss</code>, <code>.less</code>)</td>
<td>Standard CSS</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Processing model</td>
<td>Compilation (custom syntax =E2=86=92 CSS)</td>
<td>Plugin-based transformation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Extensibility</td>
<td>Built-in features only</td>
<td>Any custom plugin</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Speed</td>
<td>Slower (full parse + transpile)</td>
<td>Very fast</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Usage</td>
<td>Pre-processing</td>
<td>Post-processing (or both with <code>postcss-preset-env</code>)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common PostCSS plugins:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Plugin</th>
<th>Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>autoprefixer</code></td>
<td>Adds vendor prefixes automatically based on Browserslist</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>postcss-preset-env</code></td>
<td>Converts modern CSS (nesting, custom media, etc.) to older syntax</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>cssnano</code></td>
<td>Minifies CSS for production</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>postcss-custom-properties</code></td>
<td>Polyfills CSS custom properties for older browsers</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
