<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Critical CSS</strong> is the minimum CSS required t=
o render the <strong>above-the-fold</strong> (initially visible) content of=
 a page without any render-blocking network requests. Inlining it in the <c=
ode>&lt;head&gt;</code> eliminates the round-trip delay of an external styl=
esheet fetch, significantly improving <strong>First Contentful Paint (FCP)<=
/strong>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>The problem:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Every <code>&lt;link rel=3D"stylesheet"&gt;</code> in the <=
code>&lt;head&gt;</code> is <strong>render-blocking</strong> =E2=80=94 the =
browser will not paint anything until the full stylesheet has been download=
ed and parsed.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>The solution =E2=80=94 inline critical, load the re=
st async:</strong></p>
